      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need a step by step guide on how to roll out mfa to our whole firm using hardware keys like yubikeys instead of sms. we're a law firm so it needs to be pretty airtight but i also need to know how to explain the onboarding to people who aren't tech savvy. can u help?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! Here's a step-by-step guide for rolling out hardware MFA using YubiKeys:\n\n**Step 1: Procurement and Distribution**\n- Purchase YubiKeys in bulk, ensuring you get a secure version with encryption.\n- Collect full consent from employees and inform them about the transition and change or explanation can be simply something like, \"For security reasons, we're updating our system to better protect your information and all of our legal work.\"\n\n**Step 2: System Integration**\n- Work with your IT department (or a trusted third-party if necessary) to integrate YubiKeys with your firm's current IT infrastructure. This typically involves:\n  - Setting up the YubiKeys for each employee’s profile.\n  - Configuring the YubiKeys to pair with the employees' existing accounts.\n  - Ensuring that the system accepts the YubiKeys for MFA prompts.\n\n**Step 3: Onboarding Process**\n- Train staff on the basics of securing their YubiKey, such as flashing (if applicable) and keeping it plugged in/nearby.\n- Explain that each employee will receive their YubiKey and possibly additional YubiKey fob for their desk.\n- Emphasize that using the YubiKey is mandatory for accessing the system",
